id: pmc-txk1
title: List closed issues under Fixed only when a repair is recorded
description: "Require tracker repair evidence before classifying closed issues as Fixed; use neutral Closed entries for factual closures and omit non-change dispositions. Repro: pm-github-n0mm; classifier history: pmc-874d."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[2]: changelog,classifier
created_at: "2026-10-20T10:13:29.451Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-20T16:31:57.962Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Real-shaped classifier table, historical incident repro, full snapshot, no-git stdin and tracker input, behavioural revert proof, unchanged npm and Bun release gates, regenerated own changelog."
comments[35]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-20T10:14:19.120Z",codex-agent,"Search found no existing evidence-based closure feature; pmc-874d is historical classifier precedence work. Design: for closed Issue/Bug/Bugfix/Defect records, explicit non-change dispositions in close_reason or resolution take precedence and are excluded. Other closures require linked files/tests, explicit affirmative repair wording in close_reason/resolution, or delivered/merged PR or commit evidence in resolution/actual_result/links; otherwise render Closed: title under Closed. Type/tag/title alone is not repair evidence. Features and Tasks retain existing classification. All projections use one selection policy; JSON reports non-change exclusions. Tracker data only; preserve existing release placement and prepend history. Fixtures will use sanitized SDK/fleet field shapes, including source closure timestamps and GitHub completion wording."
  "2026-10-20T10:20:22.684Z",codex-agent,"Focused regressions pass 57/57 (zero skipped): SDK/fleet-shaped files/tests, resolution/actual_result, merged PR/commit links, affirmative and negated repair statements, all non-change disposition spellings, incident repro, full historical snapshot, deterministic reversed input, preserved prepend history, and real SDK-created no-git tracker plus stdin under empty PATH. Policy refinement: non-change dispositions apply to every closed item type; Feature/Task category behavior otherwise stays unchanged. JSON exclusion count is across input before release/status filtering, making omitted administrative closures visible without claiming a release-specific count."
  "2026-10-20T10:24:30.951Z",codex-agent,"Behavioural revert proof in a disposable source copy, rebuilt before testing: reverting only needsNeutralClosure to the previous no-gate behavior fails 3/3 selected incident, full-snapshot and no-git regressions (0 pass). Reverting only isNonChangeClosure fails 6/6 selected disposition regressions (0 pass). The working source is untouched. The original classifier precedence suite passes 12/12 with explicit repaired fixtures. SDK fixture correction: create seeds use file/test string arrays; files objects are silently ignored by runCreate, so integration tests now seed through the documented singular options."
  "2026-10-20T10:32:46.712Z",codex-agent,"The first isolated-home full npm gate reached nine existing worker-readiness failures in test/generator-redos.test.ts (startup at 5000ms, before operation CPU measurement); the closure-evidence and no-git tests passed. This reproduces the separate pmc-redos-startup-231 issue. No parser budget, watchdog, source inventory or coverage threshold is changed. Trying an unchanged readiness control with process CPU affinity restricted to one available CPU, which also makes the Node test runner schedule files serially."
  "2026-10-20T10:40:18.819Z",codex-agent,"Final review tightened delivery references: bare resolved states, delivered issue references and issue-URL fragments are not merged-PR evidence. The classifier table passes 59/59; independent link-rendering controls pass 7/7 after repaired fixtures gained explicit resolution. Final source has the unchanged 5000ms worker startup, 250ms parser CPU and 5000ms operation watchdog, and unchanged 100 percent line/branch/function coverage thresholds. README section rules and release-note docs describe evidence, dispositions, neutral prefixes and exclusion-count scope."
  "2026-10-20T10:49:35.487Z",codex-agent,"PR 262 is open at e70df9c. Final linked command node --test test/closure-evidence.test.ts passes 62/62 through pm test --run --match closure-evidence --timeout 1800 --progress (zero skipped; tracking_disabled leaves results in comments). CI on the same code commit passes all 679 tests on Node 22 and Node 26, with exact 100 percent measured lines/branches/functions across all 14 source files, 175 documented declarations, zero production vulnerabilities and all package/changelog/date/attestation checks. A literal function-only revert from the base commit was also verified in a disposable copy: reverting classifyItem fails all 3 incident/snapshot/no-git tests, and reverting filterItemsByStatus fails all 6 selected disposition tests. Both probes rebuild dist; source checksums remain unchanged. Local full npm and Bun receipts are still running separately."
  "2026-10-20T10:53:47.003Z",codex-agent,"Final review found a field-grouping bypass: section-by label could build a Fixed heading directly from a fixed tag on a neutral issue. groupSectionItems now routes neutral closures to Closed before type/status/label grouping and merges an existing Closed group rather than duplicating its heading. Added real-shaped mixed Feature/Issue projection regressions for all three grouping modes. Superseded the in-flight local gate attempts so final receipts will cover this correction; no threshold or harness limit changed."
  "2026-10-20T10:55:47.881Z",codex-agent,"The corrected focused suite passes 65/65 via the linked pm test command (zero failures/skips). Exact function-only reverts from the base commit, each in its own rebuilt disposable source copy, fail as required: classifyItem 0/3 pass, filterItemsByStatus 0/6 pass, groupSectionItems 0/2 pass for type/label bypass regressions. The fixed status-grouping regression also verifies a single merged Closed heading. Own changelog regenerated after pm writes; code, docs and release gates keep their original thresholds and budgets."
  "2026-10-20T11:16:55.252Z",codex-agent,"Final verification at code commit 51447ab: focused linked suite 65/65, existing link controls 7/7; function-only reverts fail 3/3 classifier, 6/6 selection and 2/2 grouping regressions. CI Node 22 and Node 26 each pass 682/682 with zero skipped/cancelled tests, exact 100 percent measured lines/branches/functions across all 14 sources, 175 documented declarations, zero production vulnerabilities and all release components. Full local npm release:check is 671/682 (11 unchanged readiness timeouts, pmc-redos-startup-231); full local Bun release:check is 670/682 (the same 11 plus the unchanged hostile-link wall assertion, pmc-rspo). Both local runs measure 100/100/100 and exit nonzero; they are not green gates. The extra timing case passes 1/1 with and without coverage in isolation. Audit, package dry-run, changelog drift/links, release date and publish attestation all pass separately. Source hashes stay unchanged. PM SDK UX gap encountered: runCreate accepts unknown option keys and silently ignores files objects; real fixture seeds use documented file/test string arrays instead. No PM CLI/SDK issue was filed. PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/pull/262 remains unmerged and unreleased; local validation risks stay open in their existing items."
  "2026-10-20T12:09:19.291Z",codex-agent,"Review round for PR 262: fetched every unresolved thread and all comments (3 threads; no pagination remaining), plus latest CodeRabbit review with 1 outside-diff finding. All four are valid: README neutral-title exception, disposition keyword boundaries, symptom-word false negatives, and missing GitHub Actions exclusion count. Remote branch is current and includes main. Plan: bounded disposition terminators, explicit non-delivery negation, regression fixtures and output checks, behavioural revert proofs, whole-diff self-review, unchanged npm/Bun release gates and rebuilt dist. No thread replies or resolutions."
  "2026-10-20T12:11:19.184Z",codex-agent,"Focused suite now passes 96/96 with zero skipped. Added repair-prose boundary, symptom wording, preserved explicit non-delivery and disposition controls, plus real no-git workflow output receipts for file and stdout/prepend modes. Whole-diff self-review found the same omission in text --explain diagnostics; fixed and covered it. Existing historical incident projection test verifies the README neutral-title exception. Running independent behavioural reverts and full unchanged release gates next."
  "2026-10-20T12:12:30.259Z",codex-agent,"Behavioural revert proofs completed in disposable source copies, rebuilding dist for each independent mutation; package worktree code stayed unchanged. Restoring only NON_CHANGE to the reviewed head fails 4/4 selected prose-boundary regressions; restoring only NEGATED_REPAIR fails 8/8 symptom regressions. Restoring only writeGitHubOutput fails 1/1 workflow regression; restoring only writeSelectionReport fails 1/1 diagnostics regression. Restoring only resolveEntryTitle from main fails 1/1 historical incident entry-from regression supporting the README exception. All five probes exit 1, zero skipped; fixed focused suite and linked pm execution pass 96/96. Explicit planned/proposed/unmerged/negated delivery controls remain neutral."
  "2026-10-20T12:14:58.219Z",codex-agent,"Review mapping: PRRT_kwDOSfkApc6uTu7g documents the neutral Closed title exception; PRRT_kwDOSfkApc6uTu7n bounds complete dispositions; PRRT_kwDOSfkApc6uTu8E scopes negation to explicit non-delivery while retaining planned states. Outside-diff finding 4faeccdfe28fa0c2c67c3ffc adds excluded_non_change_count to GitHub Actions output. Additional self-review fix exposes non_change in text selection diagnostics. No finding refused. Full PR source/test/docs diff reviewed; generated dist rebuilt. Isolated-HOME pm health satisfies the existing CI legacy-provenance baseline, without history repair or pin changes. Linked pm test passes 96/96; runner reports tracking_disabled, so results are recorded here."
  "2026-10-20T12:25:37.990Z",codex-agent,"Complete npm release:check on Node 26.12.0 with isolated HOME and Git configuration exits 1: 703/713 tests pass, 10 fail, zero skipped/cancelled. Every failure is the unchanged generator-redos worker startup exceeding 5000ms before parser execution (existing pmc-redos-startup-231); the full new closure suite passes. Coverage remains 100 percent lines/branches/functions across all 14 measured sources; docstrings cover 175 declarations. Audit, release-date and publish-attestation components pass separately. Running the full Bun gate with two CPUs available to reduce concurrent test files without changing thresholds, parser CPU limits or watchdogs."
  "2026-10-20T12:53:46.746Z",codex-agent,"Review fixes and self-review are complete. Full unchanged release gates: npm 703/713 (10 existing startup failures), Bun 712/713 with two CPUs available (1 existing startup failure), zero skipped/cancelled, both exit 1. All failures are generator-redos workers not starting within 5000ms before parser execution, tracked in pmc-redos-startup-231. Both runs report 100 percent lines/branches/functions across all 14 required sources and 175 documented declarations. Focused linked test passes 96/96. Independent rebuilt reverts fail 4/4 disposition, 8/8 negation, 1/1 workflow writer, 1/1 diagnostics writer and 1/1 neutral-entry control. Audit, 52-file package dry-run, release date and publish-attestation checks pass separately; earlier changelog drift/link check passes and is being rerun after final tracker writes. CI health baseline passes with isolated HOME. No coverage/timing thresholds, dependency pins or history records changed. pm test reports tracking_disabled; evidence is in these comments. No new PM CLI/SDK defect was encountered. Releasing this claim without closing either item, then regenerating/checking the changelog, committing explicit paths with rebuilt dist and tracker history, and pushing PR 262. Review threads remain untouched; no merge or package release."
  "2026-10-20T13:12:33.886Z",codex-agent,"PR 262 review round: fetched all five threads with every comment and complete pagination; two remain unresolved (PRRT_kwDOSfkApc6uVoDW and PRRT_kwDOSfkApc6uVoDd). Latest CodeRabbit review has no outside-diff findings; earlier GitHub Actions exclusion-count finding is already fixed and covered. Branch is current and includes origin/main. Both new findings are valid: explanatory dispositions leak into output, and neutral closures affect semver counts and breaking groups. Plan: preserve bounded disposition matching, exclude administrative closures from change signals, cover markdown/structured/CLI and direct SDK projections, prove independent behavioural reverts, review the full PR diff, and run unchanged npm/Bun release gates. No thread replies or resolutions."
  "2026-10-20T13:15:33.343Z",codex-agent,"Regressions pass 114/114 with zero skipped, including no-git CLI receipts, explanatory connectors, repair-prose boundary controls, all breaking signal forms, and mixed substantive fix/feature/breaking controls. Before implementation the new selected regressions failed 14/14. Independent disposable rebuilt source copies prove each fix: restoring only NON_CHANGE fails 8/8 explanatory tests; restoring only suggestSemverForItems fails 6/6 neutral/mixed tests; restoring only isBreakingItem fails 4/5 selected tests (the plain neutral control passes). All probes exit 1 with zero skips; worktree source hashes are unchanged. Whole-PR self-review also fixed direct suggestSemverForItems counting explicit non-change closures when callers pass unfiltered items; markdown and structured Breaking Changes share the guarded predicate. Latest review outside-diff inventory is empty, and earlier workflow-output finding remains covered. Running complete npm and Bun gates under isolated HOME and Git configuration; unchanged thresholds and parser budgets."
  "2026-10-20T13:18:54.082Z",codex-agent,"Additional self-review revert proof: an omitted closure with linked-file evidence must still be ignored by direct suggestSemverForItems. Removing only the explicit isNonChangeClosure guard fails the mixed substantive regression 1/1 in a rebuilt disposable copy. Strengthened control passes 1/1 with the fix. The linked pm run hit its 120-second wrapper timeout during no-git tracker setup under host load; the direct focused suite already passed 114/114, and a longer wrapper retry will retain all repository budgets. Code and regression changes are ready for CI while full isolated-home local gates continue; results will be appended before handoff."
  "2026-10-20T13:26:54.257Z",codex-agent,"Code commit 5350ec693ef3ef4ec9a27de38af7cd9e33420727 CI passes on Node 22 and Node 26: each 731/731 tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations, exact 100 percent measured lines/branches/functions across all 14 required sources, 175 documented declarations, zero production vulnerabilities, package dry-run, changelog drift/link checks, release-date and publish-attestation checks. CI run 39429507300 and CodeQL run 39429506728 both succeed. Post-commit identity/privacy tests pass 4/4; isolated-home tracker health matches the existing CI legacy-provenance baseline. Linked pm test retry passes all 114 tests in about 92 seconds with a 600-second wrapper limit, clearing the earlier 120-second wrapper timeout without changing repository test budgets. Runner result persistence remains tracking_disabled, so receipts are recorded in comments. Full local npm and Bun release gates continue sequentially with isolated HOME/Git settings and two available CPUs."
  "2026-10-20T13:45:52.022Z",codex-agent,"Final review-round verification for code commit 5350ec693ef3ef4ec9a27de38af7cd9e33420727: full npm run release:check passes 731/731 and full bun run release:check passes 731/731, both exit 0 with zero failed/skipped/cancelled tests. Both used isolated HOME and Git configuration with unchanged thresholds and parser budgets. Each measures 100 percent lines/branches/functions across all 14 required source files; docstrings cover 175 declarations. Production audit reports zero vulnerabilities; the 52-file package dry-run, changelog drift/link checks, version-derived date and publish-attestation checks pass. CI Node 22 and Node 26 also each pass 731/731, and CodeQL passes. The earlier linked-test wrapper timeout passes on retry (114/114); no local full-gate timeout remains in this round. Final semver function revert was repeated against immutable reviewed head e08fd791cb2a6c81d29d24877d0896f4bbe02a20 and fails 6/6 with final regression content; disposition revert fails 8/8, breaking predicate revert fails 4/5 (plain neutral control passes), and explicit non-change guard revert fails 1/1. Rebuilt disposable probes leave worktree source hashes unchanged. Re-fetched threads still show only PRRT_kwDOSfkApc6uVoDW and PRRT_kwDOSfkApc6uVoDd unresolved; both fixes are complete, no invalid finding refused, no new outside-diff finding. Whole-PR self-review and no-git acceptance are complete. No new PM CLI/SDK defect found; linked result storage remains tracking_disabled and evidence is in these comments. Releasing the claim without closing the feature, regenerating/checking the changelog after tracker writes, and committing/pushing final receipts. No thread reply/resolution, mention, merge or package release."
  "2026-10-20T14:13:10.829Z",codex-agent,"Review round: remote head is current and contains main. Retrieved all review threads and comments: two unresolved closure-policy findings (cannot reproduce dispositions and passive repair prose). Latest CodeRabbit review has no outside-diff findings; prior GitHub output count finding will be reverified. Plan: add behavioral regressions, audit full PR for related cases and unused declarations, prove function reverts fail, then run unchanged npm and Bun release gates with isolated git identity."
  "2026-10-20T14:15:34.671Z",codex-agent,"Both unresolved findings are valid. Added bounded cannot-reproduce dispositions, affirmative passive repair phrases and explicit hypothetical-repair guards found during whole-diff self-review. New regression selection initially failed 18/26; modal guard selection initially failed 3/6. Removed the PR-introduced unused readFileSync import in test/check-diff.test.ts; strict noUnusedLocals/noUnusedParameters through a temporary config extending tsconfig.json over all PR-changed source/test files now passes. Updated public closure-policy docs and real non-git tracker fixtures. Latest CodeRabbit body has no outside-diff findings; the older GitHub output omission remains fixed with its behavioral regression. No dependency pins or gate thresholds changed."
  "2026-10-20T14:16:15.087Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proofs: independent disposable source copies each rebuilt dist, then restored only the reviewed-head policy declaration. NON_CHANGE revert fails 9/9 selected cannot-reproduce regressions; REPAIR revert fails 9/9 passive-repair/boundary regressions; NEGATED_REPAIR revert fails 3/3 hypothetical-repair regressions. Every probe exits 1 with zero skipped. Fixed focused suite passes 146/146, and pm test pmc-txk1 --run --match 'node --test test/closure-evidence.test.ts' --progress passes 146/146. Original worktree policy stayed fixed throughout the disposable probes. Full unchanged npm/Bun release gates are running with isolated Git identity and one available CPU to limit test-file concurrency on the busy host."
  "2026-10-20T14:23:21.049Z",codex-agent,"Correction to the unused-import receipt: git show origin/main:test/check-diff.test.ts confirms readFileSync was already unused on main, so it was not introduced by this PR. It was the sole unused declaration reported across the PR-changed source/test scope and has been removed; the strict compiler check now passes. DeepScan dashboard details remain unavailable, so this is not a claim that its reported new issue has been identified or cleared."
  "2026-10-20T14:25:30.861Z",codex-agent,"Full npm run release:check passes: 763/763 tests, zero failures/skips/cancelled, 100 percent measured lines/branches/functions across all 14 required source files, 175 documented declarations, zero production vulnerabilities and the complete 52-file package dry-run plus changelog/link, date and publish-attestation checks. Run used Node 26.12.0, isolated HOME/Git configuration, unchanged thresholds/budgets and one available CPU; no retry was needed. CI-equivalent isolated tracker-health baseline and identity/privacy 4/4 pass. Full Bun gate is now running with two CPUs available, still using unchanged scripts and budgets."
  "2026-10-20T14:37:06.591Z",codex-agent,"Final review round: both npm run release:check and bun run release:check pass 763/763, zero failed/skipped/cancelled, with isolated HOME/Git configuration and unchanged thresholds/budgets. Neither full run required a retry. Both measure 100 percent lines/branches/functions across 14 required sources and 175 documented declarations; production audit has zero vulnerabilities, the 52-file package dry-run and changelog/link/date/attestation gates pass. Focused node --test test/closure-evidence.test.ts and its linked pm execution pass 146/146; independent rebuilt policy reverts fail 9/9 disposition, 9/9 passive-repair and 3/3 hypothetical-repair regressions. Strict noUnusedLocals/noUnusedParameters over every PR-changed source/test file passes after removing one pre-existing unused import from a changed test file. Identity/privacy tests pass 4/4, added-line privacy scan is clean, isolated tracker health satisfies the existing CI legacy-provenance baseline, and existing history bytes remain unchanged. Final complete review fetch still has only PRRT_kwDOSfkApc6uXP79 and PRRT_kwDOSfkApc6uXP8I unresolved; both valid findings are fixed, with no new outside-diff findings. Whole-diff self-review added hypothetical-repair guards. DeepScan dashboard-only details remain unverified. No new PM CLI/SDK defect; linked result storage remains tracking_disabled, so durable receipts are in these comments. Releasing without closing, regenerating/checking changelog, committing explicit code/dist/docs/tracker paths and pushing. No thread reply/resolution, mention, merge or release."
  "2026-10-20T15:43:14.832Z",codex-agent,"Static-analysis review round for PR 262 at 3428bee: remote branch is current and includes main. Complete GraphQL inventory has seven resolved threads, zero unresolved, and no truncated thread/comment pages. Latest substantive CodeRabbit review has no outside-diff finding; older exclusion-count output finding is already fixed and covered. Plan: temporary regexp recommended and strict type-checked lint plus no-unused compiler checks over PR-changed source/tests, verify and fix genuine new-code findings, behavioral revert proofs, whole-diff review, unchanged full npm/Bun release gates, rebuilt dist and explicit tracker/code commit. No thread replies or resolutions."
  "2026-10-20T15:46:29.896Z",codex-agent,"Static analysis completed over all 12 PR-changed source/test files using temporary no-save ESLint 10, regexp recommended and typescript-eslint strict-type-checked config. Compiler noUnusedLocals/noUnusedParameters passes. Five regexp diagnostics are in new code: redundant single-character group in NEGATED_REPAIR, redundant outer DELIVERY_REF group, and three ASCII digit-class simplifications. These are equivalent rewrites; removing unnecessary structure preserves matching. Other new-line typed lint messages are numeric interpolation, Node test registration promises, cleanup callbacks and String conversion of an internally produced numeric summary field; inspected call sites establish intentional behavior. Existing-file diagnostics outside changed code are out of scope. No duplicate class character, useless escape, unused capture or super-linear finding exists in the new policy. Verifying static red/green revert proofs and full closure behavior next."
  "2026-10-20T15:48:24.378Z",codex-agent,"Static revert proof: ESLint 10.13.0, typescript-eslint 8.72.0 and eslint-plugin-regexp 3.3.1. Fixed closure-policy has zero regexp recommended diagnostics. In-memory independent declaration reverts to 3428bee restore 1 diagnostic for NEGATED_REPAIR and 4 for DELIVERY_REF (1 redundant group plus 3 digit-class warnings); original worktree source is not mutated. Temporary Node static regression harness verifies these rule invariants; runtime-equivalent edits are checked by the unchanged behavioral closure suite, 146/146 pass with zero skipped/cancelled. No behavioral red result is claimed for equivalent regex languages. Full unchanged isolated-home npm gate is running; Bun follows. No dependency/config files or thresholds changed."
  "2026-10-20T15:52:55.621Z",codex-agent,"DeepScan stayed at 1 new / 1 fixed after the regexp cleanup. The public dashboard read API exposed the actual issue 237963432: INSUFFICIENT_NULL_CHECK at test/closure-evidence.test.ts:166-167. The semver projection loop optionally accessed suggestion.bump and then unconditionally accessed suggestion.counts. Added an explicit assert.ok(suggestion) before either property and removed optional access; this preserves successful projection behavior and produces an assertion failure for a missing optional document field. Full-diff search found no other introduced instance of this access pattern. The 5 regexp cleanups remain valid static simplifications, but were not the DeepScan issue. Current npm gate includes the same source behavior; focused checks, no-unused compiler and external scan will verify the final test edit."
  "2026-10-20T15:55:24.405Z",codex-agent,"DeepScan verification: 3428bee and regex-only code commit 6737f42 each report 1 new / 1 fixed; assertion commit 2052fe1f60686b1ba61b952454e7b3b9d714204f reports 0 new / 1 fixed. Public pull-request read receipt 2493543 has an empty newDefectIds array at that exact head. This independently confirms issue 237963432 was the inconsistent optional suggestion access in the test loop, not a regex defect. Selected semver behavior passes 1/1; strict no-unused checks pass after the assertion edit, and full release coverage has passed the closure suite. Static regex Node regression harness is 3/3 green; NEGATED_REPAIR-only revert yields 1 failing / 2 passing checks and DELIVERY_REF-only revert yields 2 failing / 1 passing checks, with no skips. Temporary lint tooling/config remains untracked outside the package. Identity/privacy passes 4/4; isolated tracker health matches the unchanged CI legacy-provenance baseline. No new PM CLI/SDK defect found; linked result storage remains tracking_disabled."
  "2026-10-20T16:01:50.070Z",codex-agent,"Out-of-scope follow-up pmc-lwfw records the three source/test DeepScan baseline diagnostics verified on origin/main (redundant stdout condition and two unused test imports). No baseline code is changed in PR 262. Latest full review fetch still has seven threads, all resolved, with complete comments and no pagination. CI at 2052fe1 passes on Node 22 and Node 26, each 763/763 tests with zero failures/skips/cancellations, exact 100 percent measured lines/branches/functions across 14 required sources, 175 documented declarations, zero production vulnerabilities and all remaining release components. Final linked closure execution passes 146/146. Local full npm and Bun gates continue sequentially with isolated HOME/Git configuration and unchanged budgets."
  "2026-10-20T16:11:11.715Z",codex-agent,"Local full npm run release:check completed with exit 1: 759/763 pass, 4 fail, zero skipped/cancelled. All four failures are existing generator-redos workers failing the unchanged 5000ms startup budget before parser execution: replace-release, insert-release, title-heading and dep-github-url. There are no parser CPU/watchdog or closure regressions. Exact final code 2052fe1 CI passes all 763/763 on both Node 22 and Node 26, including all four timeout cases and every release component. Per this round instruction these host-load timeouts are not treated as product failures. Bun full gate is now running at unchanged thresholds and budgets."
  "2026-10-20T16:12:43.769Z",codex-agent,"Local timing retry passes: taskset -c 2 node --test test/generator-redos.test.ts on Node 26.12.0 reports 11/11 pass, zero failures/skips/cancellations, exit 0. All four npm startup-timeout cases therefore pass both a local retry and exact-code CI. Startup remains 5000ms, parser operation CPU remains 250ms and wall watchdog remains 5000ms. The original complete npm receipt remains honestly recorded as exit 1 with 759/763; no thresholds or harness timeouts were changed. Full Bun release gate remains in progress."
  "2026-10-20T16:31:54.917Z",codex-agent,"Final verification for source/test commit 2052fe1f60686b1ba61b952454e7b3b9d714204f: full bun run release:check exits 0, 763/763 tests pass, zero failed/skipped/cancelled. It measures 100 percent lines/branches/functions across all 14 required source files, documents 175 declarations, reports zero production vulnerabilities, packs 52 files in dry-run, and passes changelog drift/links, release date and publish attestation. Full npm run release:check exits 1 with 759/763 and four existing 5000ms worker-startup timeouts; all 11 ReDoS checks pass on local retry with unchanged startup/CPU/watchdog budgets, and exact-code CI Node 22/26 each pass 763/763 plus all release components. This round accepts those host-load timeouts per instruction, without relabeling the initial npm exit. Final linked closure suite passes 146/146. Temporary no-unused compiler check passes; policy regexp lint is clean; static regression harness is 3/3 green and independent constant reverts fail 1/3 and 2/3 checks. DeepScan at 2052fe1 is 0 new / 1 fixed; assertion makes the semver suggestion invariant explicit. Both redundant groups and all three digit classes are equivalent rewrites. Complete review inventory remains seven resolved threads, zero unresolved; older outside-diff workflow-count fix remains covered. Baseline-only follow-up pmc-lwfw stays open. History remains append-only and privacy checks pass. No dependency pins, lint config, thresholds or test budgets changed. No new PM CLI/SDK defect; linked result storage reports tracking_disabled, with receipts retained here. Releasing the claim without closing either item, regenerating/checking changelog after tracker writes and pushing the final tracker receipt. No thread replies/resolutions, mentions, merge or release."
